5.035.74The cited references fail to disclose or suggest the features of claims 1 and 15. Seeley discloses a display assembly with a flat panel display 205 which is disposed between a front panel 210 and a back panel 215. See Seeley FIG. 2; Col. 3, lines 23-29. The front and back panels 210, 215 are rigidly coupled via an integrated cam latch which includes the plurality of "matched interlocking extensions along one edge of each of the respective front and back panels." See Seeley Col. 1, lines 46-49. The location of each of the "plurality of interlocking extensions 225 and 240 are contiguous to each other and form a latch, via the rotational coupling of the panels containing the latch." See Seeley Col. 2,
